Chapter: RocListReturned
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig,
 "inspect: list returned from function", case 18 in file order:

     { f = |_| [1, 2] result = f(0) match result { [a, b] => a + b, _ => 0 } }

 and Roc expects 3.

 A list BUILT INSIDE a function and returned, rather than passed in. The
 difference from case 17 is where the list is allocated relative to the frame
 that reads it, which for a backend with real memory is the whole question.
 Its sibling case 19 -- a closure CAPTURING a list and returning it -- is
 already ported as `roc-closure-captures-list`, and that one raised H2.

Section: Functions

  make-list : Integer -> List Integer
  make-list (ignored) = [1, 2]

  returned : Integer -> Integer
  returned (n) =
   let result = make-list 0
   in list-at result 0 + list-at result 1

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (returned 0))
  end
